course: dictionary
lesson: 7825
title: Quit: stop, leave or give up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Quit is a small word with more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Noah quit matches just before he lost so they would not count.» Here quit means stopped playing. Ask yourself what is being quit: a match, a team, a habit, or a game.
explain: Quit can mean leave a job, a school, a team or a place. It can also mean close a computer program or game, as in «Quit the game before you turn it off.» The thing being quit is the clue.
explain: Some phrases use quit in a special way. «Never quit» means do not give up. «Call it quits» means stop, or agree that nobody owes anything to anyone. When a phrase is new, read the whole phrase, not just the single word.
fact: Quit means to stop doing something, to leave a job, school, team or place, or to close a computer program or game.
fact: Quit can also mean stop a habit, such as quit smoking, which means stop smoking.
fact: «Never quit» means do not give up.
fact: «Call it quits» means stop, or agree that nobody owes anything.
fact: Quit is a verb with the forms quit, quits, quit or quitted, and quitting.
exercise: «Noah quit matches just before he lost so they would not count.» What does quit mean here? | *To stop playing | To start a new team | To run home fast | To cook a big meal
exercise: «Quit the game before you turn it off.» What does quit mean here? | To make the game louder | *To close the game | To start the game again | To win the game
exercise: What does «Never quit» mean? | Start again from the beginning | Leave early | Win every time | *Do not give up
test: «Call it quits» is a phrase that means? | *Stop, or agree that nobody owes anything | Count all the points | Join a new team | Shout very loudly
test: «A nicotine patch can make quitting easier.» Here quitting means? | Joining a club | *Stopping smoking | Winning a prize
exam: Which meaning fits «He will quit his job at the shop next month»? | Finish a game | Close a computer program | Make the job bigger | *Leave the job
